# Bug: std/regexp reads `\W`, `\D` and `\S` as the letters W, D and S.
#
# `\w`, `\d` and `\s` are supported, and their capital forms are in every
# regex dialect a programmer brings (Perl, PCRE, Go, Rust, JavaScript). An
# escape the parser does not know falls through to "the letter itself", so
# these three neither work nor fail:
#
#   expected:  o: <none>     (an o followed by a non-word character)
#   actual:    <none> oW     (an o followed by a capital W)
#
# Expected either the negated classes or an err naming the escape. The
# same fall-through makes `\q` match "q", which hides typos in patterns.
import "./probe"

print (probe/run 0)
